{
  "case": "paste-batch-one-step",
  "clause": "DESIGN R3.3 \u00a78.3 L653 paste runs C/N once for the batch; \u00a78.2 L631-L632 one normalization of the staged state and one reversible delta; L641 undo",
  "derivation": "The fixture profile plus the normalize recipe guard-duplicate-aid (N refuses any TextAnnotation other than Aid_1 whose text is [Aid] helper). One batch pastes [Aid_1] with key p4 and edits the body field of the remapped ID to copied: the state after the paste alone would make N refuse (see paste-normalize-refused), the final staged state does not, and C and N run once after the whole batch, so the batch commits. Later commands of the batch see the staged paste. The result is one history step; undo restores the initial snapshot.",
